    "evidence_text": "When a sentence is given and encoded into a vector by the encoder, the decoders are trained to predict the next sentence and the previous sentence.\n\nMethod\tOur method follows the same input format and the model architecture with original BERT.\n\nsuggest the order discrimination is essential for BERT pre-training.\n\nNote that these in-adjacent sentences will introduce much more training noise to the model.\n\n0.9, a $\\beta _2$ of 0.999 and a L2 weight decay rate of $0.01$.\n\n(IsNextInadj) label is mapped to IsPrev (IsNext) with a label smoothing factor of 0.8.\n\nwas conducted for 3 epochs for all the tasks, with a learning rate of 2e-5.\n\nThe predictions were obtained by evaluating the training checkpoint with the best validation performance.\n\nWhen comparing between PN and PN5cls, PN5cls achieves better results than PN.\n\nThis indicates that including a broader range of the context is effective for improving inference ability.\n\nSimilar to SQuAD, the system needs to extract fragments from the text as the answer.\n\nFor Chinese NLP tasks, we pre-train the model using Chinese corpus.",
